{
 "title": "IBIS-AMI optical link (C-band)",
 "group": "Photonic links",
 "description": "25 Gb/s IBIS-AMI Tx -> MZM -> 12 km C-band fiber -> PD/TIA -> IBIS-AMI Rx (CTLE + FFE + DFE + CDR)",
 "schematic": {
  "notes": [
   {
    "x": 40,
    "y": -60,
    "title": "IBIS-AMI optical link \u2014 what this testbench does",
    "lines": [
     "TX1 is an IBIS-AMI transmitter (pf_tx, 10 % post-cursor de-emphasis)",
     "driving MZM1 with 25 Gb/s PRBS-15. 12 km of C-band fiber (D = 17",
     "ps/nm/km) disperses the field; PD1 detects |E|^2, TIA1 amplifies,",
     "and RX1 is an IBIS-AMI receiver in DSP mode: adaptive CTLE, 9-tap",
     "FFE (MMSE in Init, LMS in GetWave), 4-tap DFE, Mueller-Muller CDR.",
     "",
     "The optics are simulated by circulax; the AMI models only see the",
     "electrical waveforms, as in a real optical SerDes. The Link tab's",
     "IBIS-AMI card reports the counted BER from the Rx's recovered clock,",
     "the statistical eye of the channel estimated from vrx, and the",
     "'linear fit' residual: square-law detection after dispersion is not",
     "LTI, so this is where IBIS-AMI's statistical flow starts to err.",
     "Set FIB1.length_km = 24 and watch the equalizer run out of road."
    ]
   }
  ],
